-`src/i18n/messages.js`. The server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
+`src/i18n/messages.js`; every error code has a message in both.
+
+The language comes from the request's `Accept-Language` header: the
+supported language with the highest q-value wins (header order breaks ties,
+`q=0` refuses a language), and region tags count as their language (`ko-KR`
+is `ko`). When the header is missing or names no supported language (or only
+`*`), the server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (`en` or `ko`, default `en`).
